hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27780","Haddathana Waki and Hajjaj who said: Haddathana Shuba from Simak who said: I heard Alqama ibn Wail from his father that he witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a man of Khatham called Suwayd ibn Tariq asked him about wine, and he forbade him; so he said: It is only something we make as medicine; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed it is a disease."
"27781","Haddathana Hajjaj who said: Akhbarana Shuba from Simak ibn Harb from Alqama ibn Wail from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him land; he said: So he sent Muawiya with me to give it to him, or he said: to mark it for him; he said: So Muawiya said to me: Let me ride behind you; so I said: You are not of the followers of kings; he said: So he said: Give me your sandal; so I said: Wear the shade of the she-camel; he said: So when Muawiya became caliph, I came to him and he seated me with him upon the couch and reminded me of the hadith; so Simak said: So he said: I wished I had carried him before me."
"27782","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr who said: Haddathana Israil from Simak from Alqama ibn Wail from his father who said: A woman went out to prayer, and a man met her and covered her with his clothes and fulfilled his need of her and left; and a man came upon her and she said to him: Indeed the man did to me such and such; so the man went seeking him; and a group of the Ansar came upon her and fell upon her, so she said to them: Indeed a man did to me such and such; so they went seeking him; so they brought the man who had gone seeking the man who had fallen upon her; so they took him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so she said: He is this; so when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his stoning, the one who had fallen upon her said: O Messenger of Allah, I am he; so he said to the woman: Go, for Allah has forgiven you; and he said to the man a good word; so it was said: O Prophet of Allah, will you not stone him; so he said: He has repented a repentance which, if the people of Madina had repented it, it would have been accepted of them."
